MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_001: The capital is bustling today. Now, which of these\nlovelies shall feel the wind's caress?
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_002: There you are, Syracusio. You owe me an\nexplanation!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_003: Why, hello there, Miss Olympia. An explanation?\nYou wonder about the whims of the wind, perhaps?
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_004: What? No! That is not it at all. What I want to know\nis, why have you not attempted to woo me?!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_005: You have tried to bed all of the prettiest priests\nworking at Kalla's temple...
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_006: You've even tried to woo Leilidahna and the goddess\nKalla herself...both of whom have NO interest.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_007: And yet, you've not made a single attempt to get in\nmy good graces, not to mention in my bed. ME!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_008: It's true. I am but a breeze blowing from one beauty\nto the next. And you, Olympia, are very beautiful.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_009: Oh, yes, indeed I am! Very much so!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_010: And yet... I am first and foremost a breeze that blows\nfor my lady. So, I must keep my distance from you.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_011: You are the daughter of the shrewd Lord Iris. And\nyou came to the temple to help your house flourish.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_012: For the sake of your family, you have grown and\nblossomed into the Blue Rose of Caelus.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_013: Ohohoho! Oh, Syracusio! How amusing to see YOU\ncome to such a deeply incorrect conclusion.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_014: Have I, now? I am keen to hear what this "incorrect\nconclusion" is. Please, enlighten me.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_015: My father—rather, my entire family—go to fatiguing\nlengths to ensure the house flourishes, as you say.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_016: Who they marry, how many children they have, how\nthey raise the children—every decision for the house!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_017: I, however, fled that house and escaped to the temple\nbecause I could not accept their way of thinking.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_018: I know it was selfish, but I became a priest so that\nI could live my own life...a life in pursuit of beauty.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_019: I chose my path, and I put every effort toward my\ngoal, and so I won the title Blue Rose of Caelus.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_020: I see... It seems I may not fully understand the hearts\nof women. I am sorry.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_021: I'm pleased that you, at least, understand this woman\nbetter now. Do invite me to tea someday, hmm?
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_C_022: Perhaps the Fiery Wind will have to reconsider\nin which direction it blows.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_001: Syracusio! Just as I worried you'd never ask me out,\nI discover you've been snooping into my house!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_002: I insist you explain yourself. My opinion of you may\nchange dramatically, depending on your answer.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_003: Please. Calm yourself, Miss Olympia. You put me in a\ndifficult spot when you look at me with such passion.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_004: I did not set out to scrutinize your house. Rather, I\nwas exploring matters related to the temple of Kalla.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_005: During my inquiry, I found several letters that had\nbeen sent to the temple. They bore a blue-rose seal.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_006: MY blue rose?
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_007: Indeed. The seal belongs to the house of the Blue\nRose of Caelus. Your house. Your family.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_008: Or a family closely related to yours—perhaps the\nmerchant family your sister married into.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_009: See, the temples greatly trust those who use that seal,\nand the mark gives weight to any business done.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_010: My family did not mention any of this to me. Still,\nI'm proud to have given my house this advantage.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_011: You should be. You may have started from a selfish\nplace, but your family now profits from it.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_012: At first I suspected that Lord Iris was trying to\nexploit the temple. But there was no need for worry.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_013: What I found instead is that he has been\ninstrumental in the temple's growth.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_014: Huh? So...you no longer have any concerns about\nmy house?
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_015: That is correct.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_016: Then why have you not come to me?! You have\nno reason NOT to woo me!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_017: Among the letters was a proposal. A clergyman in\nline to be the next high priest asks for your hand.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_018: *gasp*
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_020: As I am a breeze that blows only for my lady Kalla,\nyou exist in a place that I dare not tread.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_021: Miss Olympia? Are you alright?
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_022: What? Yes, yes, I am perfectly fine. I understand the\nstate of things, and I thank you for informing me.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_023: How did this happen? I have only ever wanted one\nthing...to live a beautiful life. To live MY life!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_024: And now my petals are to be plucked just as I've\nbloomed so beautifully? That...that cannot happen!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_025: There is no fleeing from this, Olympia. You have\nseized this life for yourself, and you will not run.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_B_026: Hmm...
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_001: How do you find the tea, Miss Olympia? It is elegant\nand sweet in a way that reminds me of you.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_002: Syracusio, I thought you were determined not to woo\nme—that I existed in a place you dared not tread?
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_003: That is correct. But I felt so ashamed for making you\ncry, I vowed I would make it up to you.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_004: You made me...cry? Oh! You spied on me?! Do you\nfind the tears of women entertaining?!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_005: No, not at all. I am sorry. Please, don't be too angry.\nYou're so beautiful when you're not furious.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_006: You are an insufferable flirt! But let me guess—our\nlittle tea date wasn't just about making it up to me.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_007: I am well aware of just how deeply your devotion to\nthe goddess Kalla runs.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_008: You would never trifle with a woman who'd received\na marriage proposal important to the temples.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_009: My loyalty to my lady will never waver. And that is\nprecisely why I have asked you out.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_010: Huh? Whatever do you mean?
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_011: Miss Olympia, you are strong, noble, beautiful...\na flower that blooms exactly as she chooses to.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_012: It would be of no benefit to my lady if a marriage\nproposal caused the Blue Rose of Caelus to wither.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_013: Syracusio...
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_014: When I told her of your tears, she assured me that\nshe had always intended to respect your desires.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_015: Please, allow me to apologize again. I knew full well\nyour feelings on the subject, and I still made you cry.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_016: Somewhere in my heart, I believed that one day, you\nwould go along with Lord Iris's wishes.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_017: Children always come to understand their family's\nway of thinking...or so I thought, not having a family.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_018: You are usually so perceptive. It is because I cannot\nunderstand their thinking that I felt so alone at home.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_019: My family and I, we do have a love for each other\nas people.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_020: But I was the only one who could not bear the idea\nof having children merely for the sake of the house.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_021: We must all follow our own truths and live our own\nlives, should we not?
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_022: I would think you, of all people, would understand.\nYou who was born lonely and yet totally free.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_023: Ah...
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_024: Of course, if such an offer were to come from\nyou, Syracusio, then I...I...
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_025: No, you must ask me first. You have kept me waiting\nfor such a very long time, after all.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_026: Hahaha. You are a truly selfish young woman. I am\nsorry, but the wind never stays in one place.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_027: Though, now that I think of it, the Blue Fiery\nWind has a nice ring, as far as nicknames go.
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_028: What is that supposed to mean? Come now, be\nhonest with yourself. You want to be with me!
MID_SE_Sci_Oly_A_029: Hahaha. Your imagination is a beautiful thing,\nmy dear.